                 │
                 │ AddCity()
                 ▼
          CityPresenter
                 │
        validate "Austin"
                 │
                 ▼
          CityRepository
                 │
                 │ CityExists()
                 ▼
             PostgreSQL
                 │
             not found
                 │
                 ▼
          CityRepository
                 │
            AddCity()
                 │
                 ▼
          PostgreSQL
                 │
             INSERT
                 ▼
          CityPresenter
                 │
                 ▼
           CityForm
                 │
                 ▼
       "City added successfully"
```

 That's a clean **MVP (Model–View–Presenter)** separation.

 ### One thing I'd change from your earlier code

 Your previous repository had:

```
INSERT INTO City (Name, Std, Tag)
```

 but your actual PostgreSQL table has:

```
code
ct_nm
```

 So **do not use `Name`, `Std`, or `Tag`** with this database. The correct insert is:

```
INSERT INTO city (ct_nm)
VALUES (@cityName)
```

